<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">30 October in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 30 October, from 637 to 1961.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">637 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,389 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Antioch surrenders to the Arab armies</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After the Battle of the Iron Bridge, Antioch surrendered to Muslim forces under Abu Ubayda. The fall of the great Syrian city was part of the rapid conquests that stripped Byzantium of its eastern provinces.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antioch">Antioch</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/crusade" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/crusade.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1270 CE <span class="tih-ago">756 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Treaty of Tunis ends the Eighth Crusade</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After Louis IX died of disease outside Tunis, his brother Charles of Anjou negotiated a treaty with the sultan of Tunis and the crusaders withdrew. Louis was canonised in 1297.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">Crusade</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunis">Tunis</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1485 CE <span class="tih-ago">541 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Henry VII is crowned, beginning the Tudor dynasty</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Henry Tudor was crowned at Westminster Abbey two months after defeating Richard III at Bosworth. His marriage to Elizabeth of York united the rival houses of the Wars of the Roses.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1918 CE <span class="tih-ago">108 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Armistice of Mudros takes the Ottomans out of the war</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Ottoman and British representatives signed an armistice aboard HMS Agamemnon off Lemnos. Allied occupation and partition plans followed, provoking the Turkish national movement led by Mustafa Kemal.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1938 CE <span class="tih-ago">88 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Orson Welles broadcasts The War of the Worlds</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">CBS aired Orson Welles's radio adaptation of H. G. Wells's novel as a series of mock news bulletins about a Martian landing in New Jersey. Some listeners were alarmed, though newspapers exaggerated the 'panic'.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1961 CE <span class="tih-ago">65 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Soviet Union tests the Tsar Bomba</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A Soviet bomber dropped the largest nuclear weapon ever exploded over Novaya Zemlya in the Arctic. Its yield of about 50 megatons was some 3,000 times that of the Hiroshima bomb.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hiroshima">Hiroshima</a></div></div></li></ol>
